{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '275,435p' scripts/core0_ir_v1.py && sed -n '1564,1586p' scripts/core0_ir_v1.py && sed -n '1990,2091p' scripts/core0_ir_v1.py && rg -n 'MC02|MC04|MC10|MC20|MC23|MC24' docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md\"","aggregated_output":"    name: str\n    external: str\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass EntityDecl:\n    name: str\n    currency: str\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass BookDecl:\n    name: str\n    entity: str\n    basis: str\n    version: str\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass AccountDecl:\n    name: str\n    role: str\n    book: str\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass OpeningDecl:\n    name: str\n    book: str\n    external: str\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass ObservationDecl:\n    name: str\n    type_name: str\n    instant: str\n    value: Expr\n    source: str\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass SymbolDecl:\n    name: str\n    type_name: str\n    lower: Expr\n    upper: Expr\n    reason: str\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass LetDecl:\n    name: str\n    value: Expr\n    declared_type: Optional[str] = None\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass ConstraintDecl:\n    name: str\n    expression: Expr\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass ContractDecl:\n    name: str\n    type_name: str\n    book: str\n    fields: tuple[tuple[str, Expr], ...] = ()\n\n    def __init__(self, name: str, type_name: str, book: str,\n                 fields: Mapping[str, Expr] | Sequence[tuple[str, Expr]] = ()):\n        object.__setattr__(self, \"name\", name)\n        object.__setattr__(self, \"type_name\", type_name)\n        object.__setattr__(self, \"book\", book)\n        object.__setattr__(self, \"fields\", _pairs(fields))\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass AlternativeDecl:\n    name: str\n    assumptions: tuple[Expr, ...] = ()\n\n    def __init__(self, name: str, assumptions: Sequence[Expr] = ()):\n        object.__setattr__(self, \"name\", name)\n        object.__setattr__(self, \"assumptions\", tuple(assumptions))\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass ScenarioDecl:\n    name: str\n    settings: tuple[tuple[str, Expr], ...] = ()\n\n    def __init__(self, name: str, settings: Mapping[str, Expr] | Sequence[tuple[str, Expr]] = ()):\n        object.__setattr__(self, \"name\", name)\n        object.__setattr__(self, \"settings\", _pairs(settings))\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass ReportDecl:\n    name: str\n    book: str\n    mapping: Expr\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass UnsupportedDecl:\n    kind: str\n    name: str = \"\"\n\n\nDeclaration = (UseDecl | SourceDecl | EntityDecl | BookDecl | AccountDecl | OpeningDecl |\n               ObservationDecl | SymbolDecl | LetDecl | ConstraintDecl | ContractDecl |\n               AlternativeDecl | ScenarioDecl | ReportDecl | UnsupportedDecl)\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass Program:\n    module: str\n    version: str\n    declarations: tuple[Declaration, ...] = ()\n    uses: tuple[UseDecl, ...] = ()\n\n    def __init__(self, module: str, version: str,\n                 declarations: Sequence[Declaration] = (), uses: Sequence[UseDecl] = ()):\n        if isinstance(declarations, Mapping) or isinstance(uses, Mapping):\n            raise TypeError(\"Program requires typed declarations, not an IR dictionary\")\n        object.__setattr__(self, \"module\", str(module))\n        object.__setattr__(self, \"version\", str(version))\n        object.__setattr__(self, \"declarations\", tuple(declarations))\n        object.__setattr__(self, \"uses\", tuple(uses))\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Explicit compiler bindings\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass ReadingBinding:\n    key: str\n    literal: str\n    amount: Fraction | int | str\n    currency: str\n    instant: str\n    uri: str\n    filing_id: str\n    available: str\n    ingested: str\n    reviewer: str\n    review_date: str\n    review_reason: str\n    cutoff: str\n    system_as_of: Optional[str] = None\n    prior_view: str = \"fixture:empty-view\"\n    extraction: str = \"provided-binding\"\n    action: Optional[str] = None\n\n    def __post_init__(self):\n        object.__setattr__(self, \"amount\", _fraction(self.amount))\n\n\ndef compile_program(program: Program, bindings: CompileBindings,\n                    *, source_spans: Optional[Mapping[int, Mapping[str, Any]]] = None,\n                    input_text: Optional[str] = None) -> CompileResult:\n    \"\"\"Lower a typed ``Program`` through the shared Core0.1 stages.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(program, Program):\n        raise TypeError(\"compile_program requires a Program constructed from typed declarations\")\n    input_sha256 = hashlib.sha256(input_text.encode(\"utf-8\")).hexdigest() if input_text is not None else None\n    try:\n        result = _Compiler(program, bindings, source_spans, input_text).build()\n        if input_sha256 is None:\n            input_sha256 = hashlib.sha256(json.dumps(binding_projection(program), sort_keys=True).encode()).hexdigest()\n        return CompileResult(result.ir, result.diagnostics, result.source_map, input_sha256, binding_projection(bindings))\n    except _Failure as exc:\n        return CompileResult(None, (exc.diagnostic,), MappingProxyType({}),\n                             input_sha256)\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# IR validation and exact evaluation\n\n\ndef _load_schema() -> dict[str, Any]:\n    try:\n                raise _Failure(Diagnostic(\"FamilyMembership\", \"family evidence/opening references are unknown\", row[\"id\"]))\n        for row in ir[\"scenarios\"]:\n            for driver in row[\"drivers\"]:\n                info = checker.expr(driver[\"expression\"])\n                if info[0] != \"Driver<Rate<annual_simple>>\":\n                    raise _Failure(Diagnostic(\"ScenarioType\", \"scenario driver must be a constant annual rate\", row[\"id\"]))\n        for row in ir[\"reportMappings\"]:\n            if not row[\"rows\"] or row[\"rows\"][0][\"expression\"] not in checker.memo:\n                raise _Failure(Diagnostic(\"ReportMapping\", \"report mapping expression is not compiled\", row[\"id\"]))\n            rb = next((r for r in bindings.reports if r.key == row[\"id\"] or r.mapping == row[\"rows\"][0].get(\"value\")), None)\n            if row[\"book\"] not in books or row[\"basis\"] not in package_rows or not row[\"required_operations\"]:\n                raise _Failure(Diagnostic(\"ReportMapping\", \"report mapping book/package/operations are incomplete\", row[\"id\"]))\n            if rb is None:\n                # The generated mapping uses a SourceRef literal; compare the\n                # text payload directly when an explicit row binding exists.\n                expr = next((e for e in ir[\"expressions\"] if e[\"id\"] == row[\"rows\"][0][\"expression\"]), None)\n                if expr is None or expr[\"type\"] != \"SourceRef\" or expr[\"text\"] not in {r.mapping for r in bindings.reports}:\n                    raise _Failure(Diagnostic(\"ReportMapping\", \"report mapping is not bound to an explicit export\", row[\"id\"]))\n        if not ir[\"diagnostics\"]:\n            pass\n    except _Failure as exc:\n        return ValidationResult(False, (exc.diagnostic,))\n    return ValidationResult(True, ())\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass _Symbolic:\n    name: str\n\n\ndef evaluate_expression(ir: Mapping[str, Any], identifier: str,\n                        symbols: Mapping[str, Fraction | int | str] | None = None) -> Any:\n    \"\"\"Evaluate exact supported expressions for a supplied symbol assignment.\"\"\"\n    nodes = {e[\"id\"]: e for e in ir.get(\"expressions\", [])}\n    symbol_values = {k: _fraction(v) for k, v in (symbols or {}).items()}\n    observations = {o[\"id\"]: o for o in ir.get(\"observations\", [])}\n    contexts = {c[\"id\"]: c for c in ir.get(\"contexts\", [])}\n    seen: set[str] = set()\n\n    def go(eid: str) -> Any:\n        if eid in seen:\n            raise ValueError(f\"expression cycle at {eid}\")\n        if eid not in nodes:\n            raise KeyError(eid)\n        e = nodes[eid]; op = e[\"op\"]\n        if op == \"literal\":\n            if e[\"rational\"] is not None:\n                return parse_rational(e[\"rational\"])\n            if e[\"type\"] == \"Bool\":\n                return e[\"text\"] == \"true\"\n            return e[\"text\"]\n        seen.add(eid)\n        try:\n            if op == \"ref\":\n                target = e[\"target\"]\n                if target in nodes:\n                    return go(target)\n                if target in symbol_values:\n                    return symbol_values[target]\n                if target in observations:\n                    return parse_rational(observations[target][\"domain\"][\"lower\"])\n                return _Symbolic(target)\n            if op == \"call\":\n                value = go(e[\"args\"][0])\n                return value\n            args = [go(a) for a in e[\"args\"]]\n            if any(isinstance(a, _Symbolic) for a in args):\n                return _Symbolic(eid)\n            if op == \"add\": return args[0] + args[1]\n            if op == \"subtract\": return args[0] - args[1]\n            if op == \"multiply\": return args[0] * args[1]\n            if op == \"divide\": return args[0] / args[1]\n            if op == \"negate\": return -args[0]\n            if op == \"not\": return not args[0]\n            if op == \"and\": return args[0] and args[1]\n            if op == \"or\": return args[0] or args[1]\n            return {\"eq\": args[0] == args[1], \"ne\": args[0] != args[1], \"lt\": args[0] < args[1],\n                    \"le\": args[0] <= args[1], \"gt\": args[0] > args[1], \"ge\": args[0] >= args[1]}[op]\n        finally:\n            seen.remove(eid)\n    return go(identifier)\n\n\ndef semantic_projection(ir: Mapping[str, Any] | None) -> Optional[dict[str, Any]]:\n    if ir is None:\n        return None\n    # Source offsets live in CompileResult.source_map.  IR itself retains\n    # source context, package locks, assumptions, alternatives and bindings.\n    projected = copy.deepcopy(dict(ir))\n    projected.pop(\"diagnostics\", None)\n    return projected\n\n\n__all__ = [\n    \"AccountDecl\", \"AlternativeDecl\", \"ArrayExpr\", \"AssumptionBinding\", \"Binary\", \"BookDecl\",\n    \"Call\", \"CompileBindings\", \"CompileResult\", \"ConstraintDecl\", \"ContractDecl\", \"Diagnostic\",\n    \"EntityDecl\", \"Expr\", \"External\", \"LetDecl\", \"Literal\", \"OpeningBinding\", \"OpeningDecl\",\n    \"ObservationDecl\", \"PackageBinding\", \"Program\", \"RecordExpr\", \"Ref\", \"ReportBinding\",\n    \"ReportDecl\", \"ScenarioDecl\", \"SourceDecl\", \"SymbolDecl\", \"Unary\", \"UnsupportedDecl\", \"UseDecl\",\n    \"ValidationResult\", \"compile_program\", \"evaluate_expression\", \"rational\", \"semantic_projection\",\n    \"validate_ir\",\n]\n56:| MC02 | Preserve numeric meaning: entities, perimeter, concept, dimensions, currency, units, scale, sign, basis and precision. U1, D. | Complete context/value types and compatibility rules, with valid/invalid examples and faithful rendering of the original disclosed amounts. | Specified in Chs. 3, 7 and Core 0 Context/Domain/Posting records, including display and rounding metadata. Schema, source scales and rounded-debt calculations have bounded checks; bounded debt context/type/source-binding checks and schema-valid rejection cases now pass. General context/type validation remains incomplete. G2, G3, G12. |\n58:| MC04 | Separate reported assertions, extraction readings, derivations, assumptions and conflicts. U1, U2, P, D. | Define source/derived/assumed status propagation and conflict handling; show both extraction error and a genuinely conflicting disclosure without silently changing either source. | Specified source/assumption constraints, review actions and conflict sets in Chs. 3, 6, 10. The 720-to-120 OCR repair differs from the 120-to-110 reported correction; transitive invalidation has a reference check. Bounded debt acceptance/source/assumption links are now checked; full workflow validation remains pending. G2, G15, G17. |\n69:| MC10 | Distinguish uncertainty about facts, disclosure readings, admissible accounting treatment, estimates, behaviour and future shocks. U2, P, D. | Specify the categories, dependencies and admissibility checks; show why a factual unknown, permitted election and unsupported treatment cannot be substituted for one another. | Specified six uncertainty kinds with separate admission/provenance/dependency rules in Core 0 and Chs. 6–8. Examples distinguish factual composition, permitted inventory election and unsupported treatment. Factual/assumption admission is now tested for the authored debt case; all-category semantic validation remains pending. G6, G15. |\n89:| MC20 | Support materially different industry and company concepts without bypassing the common accounting semantics. U1, D. | Specify extension points, concept mappings and rule admissibility; include representative industry differences and an invalid company override. | Specified extension points, override admission, separate books and mappings in Chs. 3, 7, 9/Core 0. Inventory/bank/insurer structures expose distinct state requirements. Full invalid-override and package-conformance execution remains pending. G2, G7, G12. |\n97:| MC23 | Explain the DSL's role and tradeoffs against credible alternatives, including typed ordinary code, XBRL, ledgers, rule languages and probabilistic tools. U1, U3, P. | Tie each claimed benefit to the same concrete tasks and shared semantic requirements; state costs and a fair authoring comparison protocol. Keep empirical superiority unclaimed until evaluated. | Specified shared-IR comparison and identical authoring tasks in Chs. 5, 11/Core 0; limited syntax/literal equivalence checked. Participant study, full frontend equivalence and any superiority claim remain unevaluated. G2, G9. |\n98:| MC24 | Specify the core language and IR completely enough for compatible independent implementations. U3, D. | Provide complete grammar/lexical rules, AST/IR schemas, types, context rules, built-ins, errors, package interfaces and source-to-IR-to-result fixtures, including the demonstration package. | Core 0 grammar, closed structural IR, built-ins, arities, context/domain rules and complete debt dependency package supplied. Authored expected IR and selected expression-to-result checks pass. A frozen 17-export registry and bounded debt static validator now pass positive and schema-valid negative cases. General compilation, package loading, remaining semantic conformance and independent implementability assessment remain open. G2, G12, G15. |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
